Confocal microscopy and image analysis
For imaging of fixed cells expressing fluorescent proteins, cells grown on coverslips were fixed with 2% formaldehyde or 4% paraformaldehyde (PFA) for 15 min at room temperature and washed three times with PBS. Fixed cells were stained with or without lipid dyes according to the experimental design and mounted with Fluoromount-G. For LDs staining, cells were incubated with PBS containing 1 μg/mL of Bodipy 493/503 or LipidTox or Lipi-blue for 1 h. For immunostaining in
Fig. 4H
